1
00:00:03,645 --> 00:00:04,613
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

2
00:00:04,613 --> 00:00:06,014
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

3
00:00:06,014 --> 00:00:07,082
(Scenes with child actors
followed production guidelines.)

4
00:00:10,085 --> 00:00:12,921
(Mat Story)

5
00:00:13,822 --> 00:00:15,958
I just need to sign my name here, right?

6
00:00:17,926 --> 00:00:19,127
Please sign here.

7
00:00:20,128 --> 00:00:22,397
Once you make the move,

8
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:24,933
persuading the villagers
will only be a matter of time.

9
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,970
We'll make sure you're well taken care of.

10
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:44,252
We've set aside $300,000...

11
00:00:46,455 --> 00:00:47,889
as an incentive for you,
including the land.

12
00:00:51,059 --> 00:00:54,396
This is well above the market value.

13
00:01:00,836 --> 00:01:03,038
Cash, of course.

14
00:01:03,305 --> 00:01:04,940
We can't leave a trace.

15
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:06,475
It'll be clean and simple for both sides.

16
00:01:07,009 --> 00:01:08,076
And you know, right?

17
00:01:08,577 --> 00:01:09,778
There's a fee.

18
00:01:11,013 --> 00:01:11,947
Thirty percent.

19
00:01:40,509 --> 00:01:42,210
It's done.

20
00:01:44,079 --> 00:01:45,047
Okay.

21
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:52,955
It's over.

22
00:02:08,003 --> 00:02:08,837
Mr. Seong.

23
00:02:09,871 --> 00:02:10,639
What?

24
00:02:11,206 --> 00:02:13,175
It's over.

25
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:20,816
What are you two up to?

26
00:02:21,483 --> 00:02:23,051
Sell the land of Yeonri-ri to you?

27
00:02:26,722 --> 00:02:29,658
We wouldn't sell you
even a worthless scrap.

28
00:02:39,501 --> 00:02:40,602
You think it'll work?

29
00:02:41,503 --> 00:02:42,504
Unbelievable.

30
00:03:00,389 --> 00:03:02,257
This isn't something
to handle emotionally.

31
00:03:02,791 --> 00:03:03,825
It's company business.

32
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:06,028
Please, Chief.

33
00:03:10,198 --> 00:03:12,701
(My office by midnight)

34
00:03:13,869 --> 00:03:15,704
Tell me. What are you up to?

35
00:03:21,009 --> 00:03:21,910
The compensation plan.

36
00:03:22,411 --> 00:03:23,445
It's all fake.

37
00:03:25,447 --> 00:03:26,915
The moment you sign it,

38
00:03:27,249 --> 00:03:29,618
it's designed to trap you with no way out.

39
00:03:30,152 --> 00:03:32,788
I had to buy time
without Mr. Choi noticing.

40
00:03:32,788 --> 00:03:35,290
I can't have you go through
what happened ten years ago again.

41
00:03:37,459 --> 00:03:38,860
I trusted you.

42
00:03:39,795 --> 00:03:42,764
I never doubted you. Not even once.

43
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:52,574
Here she comes.

44
00:03:53,475 --> 00:03:55,010
Just sell your land, Chief.

45
00:03:55,477 --> 00:03:56,979
Go ahead and buy my land.

46
00:03:57,245 --> 00:03:58,947
I'll go bring it. Just wait here.

47
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:00,048
I'll go find it.

48
00:04:05,287 --> 00:04:06,922
- I'm going crazy here.
- No, I'll go.

49
00:04:06,922 --> 00:04:07,923
What's this?

50
00:04:07,923 --> 00:04:09,691
This? Put this...

51
00:04:09,691 --> 00:04:11,326
If anyone sees this, they'll take it.

52
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:13,695
So don't ever take it out, okay?

53
00:04:16,131 --> 00:04:18,300
Mr. Jeong is on his way here.

54
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,202
We must make sure
he reports it to Mr. Choi.

55
00:04:20,202 --> 00:04:22,537
I got it. How many times
do you have to tell me?

56
00:04:22,537 --> 00:04:23,939
Just act angry like you normally do.

57
00:04:23,939 --> 00:04:25,440
But don't overreact.

58
00:04:26,875 --> 00:04:27,976
Here he comes.

59
00:04:28,844 --> 00:04:30,445
Take my land.

60
00:04:31,046 --> 00:04:32,047
Set up the meeting then.

61
00:04:35,584 --> 00:04:36,485
Mr. Choi.

62
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:38,420
I think he's been persuaded.

63
00:04:39,321 --> 00:04:41,356
The chief is going to sell his land.

64
00:04:43,725 --> 00:04:45,327
We just need to take down
Mr. Choi now, right?

65
00:04:46,361 --> 00:04:47,329
In life,

66
00:04:47,863 --> 00:04:49,331
you reap what you sow.

67
00:04:50,065 --> 00:04:51,366
It's time to show that to him.

68
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:02,511
Mr. Seong, can you take responsibility
for this?

69
00:05:04,646 --> 00:05:07,149
This is a recording of you just now
proposing an under-the-table deal...

70
00:05:07,149 --> 00:05:09,284
and even asking for a kickback.

71
00:05:10,419 --> 00:05:12,888
Cash, of course.

72
00:05:12,888 --> 00:05:14,456
We can't leave a trace.

73
00:05:15,357 --> 00:05:16,625
And you know, right?

74
00:05:16,625 --> 00:05:18,060
There's a fee.

75
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,027
Thirty percent.

76
00:05:19,594 --> 00:05:22,798
It looks like you should be the one
taking responsibility, Mr. Choi.

77
00:05:29,004 --> 00:05:32,841
These people are trying to turn me
into some kind of criminal.

78
00:05:36,945 --> 00:05:39,615
Mr. Seong, you're being short-sighted.

79
00:05:39,615 --> 00:05:42,517
How can this be any proof?

80
00:06:01,803 --> 00:06:02,704
Mr. Bae.

81
00:06:03,972 --> 00:06:04,940
Who's going to explain...

82
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,276
this situation?

83
00:06:12,347 --> 00:06:13,949
We can't leave a trace.

84
00:06:13,949 --> 00:06:15,484
It'll be clean and simple for both sides.

85
00:06:18,387 --> 00:06:20,756
If what I just heard is true,

86
00:06:21,356 --> 00:06:22,991
it could be considered a breach of trust.

87
00:06:24,326 --> 00:06:26,628
But this alone
isn't sufficient evidence, Mr. Seong.

88
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:30,165
But sir, this is clearly collusion.

89
00:06:30,165 --> 00:06:31,233
The third factory...

90
00:06:32,234 --> 00:06:34,403
is a project the company's survival
depends on.

91
00:06:35,003 --> 00:06:38,540
We can't jeopardize it
over unclear suspicions.

92
00:06:40,575 --> 00:06:41,810
You heard him, right, Mr. Seong?

93
00:06:42,144 --> 00:06:43,478
Stop wasting time...

94
00:06:43,478 --> 00:06:46,281
and sign the crop unsuitability report.

95
00:06:49,885 --> 00:06:52,788
Bring the signed report
to the board first.

96
00:06:56,291 --> 00:06:59,428
As for the breach-of-trust case,
we'll discuss it...

97
00:07:00,462 --> 00:07:01,663
when you bring solid physical evidence.

98
00:07:06,735 --> 00:07:08,470
That's a very wise decision, sir.

99
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:17,613
Solid physical evidence...

100
00:07:21,450 --> 00:07:23,218
This is livestock land.

101
00:07:23,218 --> 00:07:24,786
But he's the only one
who's not from this village.

102
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,588
That land?

103
00:07:26,955 --> 00:07:28,991
The ownership changed about ten years ago.

104
00:07:29,658 --> 00:07:31,660
Did you set up a separate meeting
with him?

105
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,061
Not yet.

106
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,949
Even in that situation,

107
00:07:55,017 --> 00:07:57,486
he was smiling and playing it cool
in front of his boss. He's something.

108
00:07:59,221 --> 00:08:01,156
You did well. Relax your face.

109
00:08:03,225 --> 00:08:06,395
Maybe I was too hasty.

110
00:08:08,030 --> 00:08:11,066
Like Mr. Bae said, I should've secured
more concrete evidence.

111
00:08:13,468 --> 00:08:15,537
They've been preparing this for ten years.

112
00:08:15,537 --> 00:08:16,905
How could we beat them in one shot?

113
00:08:17,606 --> 00:08:20,542
I need to talk to Noh Hyeon Gap once more.

114
00:08:21,843 --> 00:08:23,645
Where did that rat disappear to?

115
00:08:24,313 --> 00:08:26,748
He couldn't have gone far
from the livestock shed.

116
00:08:27,115 --> 00:08:30,218
There must be a reason
he's been staying around here for years.

117
00:08:36,158 --> 00:08:37,092
Good work.

118
00:08:42,497 --> 00:08:49,071
(Final Episode
If You Plant It, It'll Definitely Grow!)

119
00:08:49,071 --> 00:08:51,673
(Mat Story)

120
00:08:53,008 --> 00:08:54,209
Unbelievable.

121
00:08:58,413 --> 00:09:00,282
Come on. Answer.

122
00:09:00,849 --> 00:09:03,685
Come on. Why won't he answer?

123
00:09:10,592 --> 00:09:12,961
Why isn't he picking up
at times like this?

124
00:09:12,961 --> 00:09:14,262
That punk.

125
00:09:14,529 --> 00:09:16,198
Lock the office doors for now...

126
00:09:16,198 --> 00:09:17,666
and don't let anyone come near.

127
00:09:18,367 --> 00:09:19,368
Unbelievable.

128
00:09:19,368 --> 00:09:20,168
(Yeonri-ri)

129
00:10:10,786 --> 00:10:12,521
What were you looking for earlier?

130
00:10:15,357 --> 00:10:16,224
Goodness.

131
00:10:16,825 --> 00:10:18,427
After ruining Yeonri-ri like that,

132
00:10:18,427 --> 00:10:20,128
you should've gone back to Seoul
and lived comfortably.

133
00:10:20,128 --> 00:10:21,530
Why did you come back here?

134
00:10:23,265 --> 00:10:24,266
I wanted...

135
00:10:24,967 --> 00:10:26,101
to set things right.

136
00:10:26,635 --> 00:10:29,738
You said you didn't want to repeat
the same mistake, right?

137
00:10:30,939 --> 00:10:34,009
Then why did you side with Mr. Choi?

138
00:10:34,009 --> 00:10:35,043
What do you mean?

139
00:10:35,043 --> 00:10:36,244
Then or now,

140
00:10:36,979 --> 00:10:38,747
I was never on Mr. Choi's side.

141
00:10:40,382 --> 00:10:41,550
What happened ten years ago...

142
00:10:43,251 --> 00:10:45,120
I never expected it
to be resolved that way.

143
00:10:45,587 --> 00:10:48,090
Since then, I haven't had
a proper night's sleep.

144
00:10:51,927 --> 00:10:55,297
I felt deeply guilty
toward the villagers...

145
00:10:57,633 --> 00:10:59,201
because I was the one in charge.

146
00:11:03,305 --> 00:11:05,707
So what?

147
00:11:05,707 --> 00:11:07,276
Not sleeping well for ten years
is all you've got?

148
00:11:07,276 --> 00:11:08,410
What exactly did you do here?

149
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:14,883
(Simwoo-myeon, Yeonri-ri)

150
00:11:24,493 --> 00:11:26,795
What do you mean you're watching him?

151
00:11:26,795 --> 00:11:28,797
You think I put you there just to watch?

152
00:11:28,797 --> 00:11:29,865
Unbelievable.

153
00:11:30,899 --> 00:11:32,901
Seong Tae Hun, in the report...

154
00:11:32,901 --> 00:11:35,304
- Spying on me...
- Do it properly this time.

155
00:11:35,304 --> 00:11:36,605
was part of your cover too?

156
00:11:38,373 --> 00:11:40,943
I haven't found any clear evidence yet.

157
00:11:42,577 --> 00:11:43,512
As for watching you...

158
00:11:44,079 --> 00:11:45,948
I needed to be sure...

159
00:11:46,848 --> 00:11:48,183
you were someone I could trust.

160
00:11:55,123 --> 00:11:58,093
I'll be coming down next week,
so stand by.

161
00:11:58,627 --> 00:12:01,563
I'll be there this Thursday,
so leave the office unlocked.

162
00:12:02,364 --> 00:12:03,265
What?

163
00:12:04,466 --> 00:12:07,803
Mr. Choi has been coming
to Yeonri-ri often.

164
00:12:08,670 --> 00:12:10,005
Why in the world would he come here?

165
00:12:10,005 --> 00:12:12,741
You startled me.
You didn't have to scream.

166
00:12:14,042 --> 00:12:15,110
I don't know why.

167
00:12:15,377 --> 00:12:17,980
Every time he came, he told me to leave.

168
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:19,781
But one thing's clear.

169
00:12:21,316 --> 00:12:23,719
There's something here.

170
00:12:36,632 --> 00:12:37,532
Hye Sun.

171
00:12:38,033 --> 00:12:39,668
I don't trust people anymore.

172
00:12:40,002 --> 00:12:42,304
Mr. Seong can't do this to us.

173
00:12:44,273 --> 00:12:45,540
We can't blame him.

174
00:12:46,408 --> 00:12:48,110
We have to fix our own situation.

175
00:12:49,811 --> 00:12:50,879
You're too nice.

176
00:12:51,647 --> 00:12:53,915
If I see him again, I'll tear him apart.

177
00:13:03,158 --> 00:13:04,092
Chief.

178
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:07,529
This must be really hard on you.
You've lost so much weight.

179
00:13:08,297 --> 00:13:09,931
That Seong Tae Hun...

180
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:13,702
He isn't the problem anymore.

181
00:13:14,236 --> 00:13:15,070
To be honest,

182
00:13:16,438 --> 00:13:17,539
he's on our side.

183
00:13:27,182 --> 00:13:29,551
I'm Choi Yeong Heon.

184
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:32,521
I'm...

185
00:13:34,022 --> 00:13:35,023
Choi Yeong Heon.

186
00:14:27,743 --> 00:14:29,077
(Yeonri-ri Specialized Cabbage
Genetic Marker Analysis Table)

187
00:15:02,411 --> 00:15:03,278
I don't know what it is.

188
00:15:04,446 --> 00:15:07,349
I can't even tell if we're looking
for a document or something physical.

189
00:15:09,251 --> 00:15:11,987
We need to figure out what we're even
supposed to be looking for first.

190
00:15:14,189 --> 00:15:16,058
I'm most suspicious about this.

191
00:15:16,058 --> 00:15:17,125
It won't even open.

192
00:15:17,859 --> 00:15:19,695
Maybe I should take it to Dong Sik.

193
00:15:21,296 --> 00:15:22,597
There must be a reason...

194
00:15:22,597 --> 00:15:25,467
Noh Hyeon Gap couldn't find it
for so long.

195
00:15:27,269 --> 00:15:30,138
Let's wrap up for today
and search again tomorrow.

196
00:15:30,505 --> 00:15:31,473
Okay?

197
00:15:31,473 --> 00:15:32,574
I'm so tired.

198
00:15:34,710 --> 00:15:36,511
(Wang Dong Hardware)

199
00:15:36,511 --> 00:15:40,248
(I'm out of the office. Please call)

200
00:15:53,462 --> 00:15:54,363
What's in it?

201
00:15:55,564 --> 00:15:57,633
Something's rattling inside.

202
00:15:57,633 --> 00:15:58,567
Open it.

203
00:16:00,202 --> 00:16:02,571
It's rusted shut. I can't open it.

204
00:16:02,571 --> 00:16:03,805
Maybe I can cut it open.

205
00:16:05,374 --> 00:16:06,441
Then do it.

206
00:16:06,875 --> 00:16:07,743
Cut it open?

207
00:16:11,947 --> 00:16:14,683
I'll get to use my strength for once.

208
00:16:20,322 --> 00:16:21,723
I'll get started now.

209
00:16:21,723 --> 00:16:22,557
Okay.

210
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:41,243
There's nothing in here. That stinks.

211
00:16:43,612 --> 00:16:44,546
Dong Sik.

212
00:16:47,149 --> 00:16:49,818
If you had something more important
than your life,

213
00:16:50,452 --> 00:16:51,553
where would you hide it?

214
00:16:54,990 --> 00:16:55,991
That's a secret.

215
00:17:31,627 --> 00:17:33,695
What was that? Was that you?

216
00:17:33,695 --> 00:17:34,963
- The bathroom.
- What?

217
00:17:34,963 --> 00:17:36,031
The bathroom.

218
00:17:36,031 --> 00:17:36,932
The bathroom?

219
00:17:37,699 --> 00:17:38,567
What's going on here?

220
00:17:40,302 --> 00:17:43,171
I didn't do it on purpose.

221
00:17:43,905 --> 00:17:45,507
I left my phone there,

222
00:17:45,507 --> 00:17:46,842
and it ended up like this.

223
00:17:48,176 --> 00:17:49,544
This place is flimsy.

224
00:17:50,012 --> 00:17:52,948
Why don't you just
break the entire wall down?

225
00:17:52,948 --> 00:17:54,149
Were you hurt?

226
00:17:54,683 --> 00:17:56,752
No, I wasn't, but...

227
00:17:57,319 --> 00:17:59,254
I can fix this.

228
00:18:02,424 --> 00:18:03,292
Once I put it back in...

229
00:18:04,426 --> 00:18:05,927
See?

230
00:18:11,633 --> 00:18:12,534
I found it.

231
00:18:14,136 --> 00:18:15,237
Honey.

232
00:18:22,678 --> 00:18:24,713
Why isn't he answering his phone?

233
00:18:29,451 --> 00:18:31,720
Unbelievable.

234
00:18:32,287 --> 00:18:33,889
I'll just go beat him up.

235
00:18:45,867 --> 00:18:48,370
Does anyone know how hard it was
for me to get to where I am?

236
00:18:49,571 --> 00:18:50,539
Unbelievable.

237
00:18:54,776 --> 00:18:57,446
I got you now.

238
00:20:11,253 --> 00:20:12,120
I found it.

239
00:20:19,861 --> 00:20:20,996
Why isn't it here?

240
00:20:28,370 --> 00:20:29,471
Are you looking for this?

241
00:20:43,218 --> 00:20:45,988
Wow. Mr. Seong Tae Hun.

242
00:20:47,222 --> 00:20:48,790
How did you even find this?

243
00:20:50,359 --> 00:20:51,793
This is about the same level...

244
00:20:52,427 --> 00:20:56,098
as when my younger son gets into trouble.

245
00:20:58,333 --> 00:21:00,502
This is aggravated theft.

246
00:21:00,502 --> 00:21:02,971
I can hand you over to the police...

247
00:21:02,971 --> 00:21:04,339
I'll give it back to you, Mr. Choi.

248
00:21:09,278 --> 00:21:10,145
Wait a minute.

249
00:21:12,147 --> 00:21:13,115
Wait a minute.

250
00:21:14,082 --> 00:21:14,983
Was it this?

251
00:21:17,419 --> 00:21:18,253
This one.

252
00:21:27,229 --> 00:21:29,064
There were some pretty interesting
documents in here.

253
00:21:29,064 --> 00:21:31,400
Like...

254
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,069
slush fund records?

255
00:21:35,504 --> 00:21:38,040
Is my name on the USB or something?

256
00:21:39,741 --> 00:21:42,911
You used your cousin
Kang Sang Jin's name...

257
00:21:42,911 --> 00:21:44,179
as a front.

258
00:21:44,846 --> 00:21:46,915
I need your help.

259
00:21:46,915 --> 00:21:49,551
I need to find out who Kang Sang Jin,
the owner of the livestock land, is.

260
00:21:49,551 --> 00:21:52,254
I'm sure there's a connection to Mr. Choi.

261
00:21:54,823 --> 00:21:55,657
(Officer Park Soon Kyung)

262
00:21:55,657 --> 00:21:56,591
Hey, Soon Kyung.

263
00:21:56,591 --> 00:21:58,894
Have you ever seen someone from Seoul
come to the livestock shed?

264
00:21:59,761 --> 00:22:02,130
Hello. I'd like to ask you something.

265
00:22:02,397 --> 00:22:03,799
(Land Register, Kang Sang Jin)

266
00:22:03,799 --> 00:22:04,800
(Property Registration, Kang Sang Jin)

267
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:05,701
(Delegated to Choi Yeong Heon)

268
00:22:05,701 --> 00:22:07,402
(Kang Sang Jin, Transaction Records)

269
00:22:07,703 --> 00:22:10,472
I confirmed that he's
Mr. Choi's maternal cousin.

270
00:22:10,872 --> 00:22:12,608
He just lent his name.

271
00:22:13,609 --> 00:22:14,443
I knew it.

272
00:22:15,677 --> 00:22:18,146
He used Noh Hyeon Gap
to disguise it as a livestock land,

273
00:22:18,146 --> 00:22:20,382
and carried out
all kinds of dirty schemes.

274
00:22:22,718 --> 00:22:24,853
I've already verified
all the transactions...

275
00:22:24,853 --> 00:22:26,989
and cross-checked everything.

276
00:22:28,557 --> 00:22:30,225
If we run digital forensics,

277
00:22:30,792 --> 00:22:33,962
we can trace the entire flow.

278
00:22:40,369 --> 00:22:41,236
Mr. Seong.

279
00:22:41,737 --> 00:22:42,771
You need money, right?

280
00:22:43,238 --> 00:22:45,741
Let's make a deal. Okay?

281
00:22:45,741 --> 00:22:48,143
I'll take care of your company loan
right away.

282
00:22:48,443 --> 00:22:50,646
Let's bury it.

283
00:22:50,646 --> 00:22:51,446
Okay?

284
00:22:52,281 --> 00:22:55,550
Do you think these puppets
can even think properly?

285
00:22:56,451 --> 00:22:57,786
With just a flick of my hand,

286
00:22:57,786 --> 00:23:01,723
I control these people's lives.

287
00:23:02,190 --> 00:23:03,525
You can do it too.

288
00:23:04,426 --> 00:23:05,961
Just have the courage.

289
00:23:07,329 --> 00:23:09,064
That sounds good.

290
00:23:09,064 --> 00:23:11,466
Shall we do it?

291
00:23:11,466 --> 00:23:12,467
Yes.

292
00:23:12,467 --> 00:23:13,335
Yes!

293
00:23:17,139 --> 00:23:18,106
Let go!

294
00:23:18,106 --> 00:23:19,474
Let go.

295
00:23:28,050 --> 00:23:30,452
(Chief)

296
00:23:30,719 --> 00:23:33,855
Let's see if there's anywhere left
to run in Yeonri-ri.

297
00:23:35,557 --> 00:23:36,625
I'm off now.

298
00:23:37,926 --> 00:23:39,227
Let's do this.

299
00:23:41,363 --> 00:23:44,232
Hye Sun, I'm not holding back today.
Don't try to stop me.

300
00:23:45,100 --> 00:23:47,469
I'm dying to punch someone too.

301
00:23:48,670 --> 00:23:51,373
Let's break through the obstacles
in Yeonri-ri today.

302
00:23:51,707 --> 00:23:53,475
Let's rip out that poisonous root
once and for all.

303
00:23:53,475 --> 00:23:55,978
- Rip out!
- Break through!

304
00:23:55,978 --> 00:23:57,312
Come out!

305
00:24:01,883 --> 00:24:05,320
- Rip out!
- Break through!

306
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:08,156
- Rip out!
- Break through!

307
00:24:08,156 --> 00:24:10,359
- A beating.
- Is the solution.

308
00:24:10,359 --> 00:24:12,527
- If we fight.
- We win.

309
00:24:12,527 --> 00:24:13,428
A beating.

310
00:24:13,428 --> 00:24:15,597
Is the whole village coming out?

311
00:24:16,031 --> 00:24:17,099
Assemble.

312
00:24:18,066 --> 00:24:19,368
- If we fight.
- We win.

313
00:24:19,368 --> 00:24:20,369
- A beating.
- Is the solution.

314
00:24:20,369 --> 00:24:22,170
- If we fight.
- We win.

315
00:24:22,170 --> 00:24:24,673
- A beating.
- Is the solution.

316
00:24:27,643 --> 00:24:29,378
- A beating.
- Is the solution.

317
00:24:29,378 --> 00:24:31,246
- If we fight.
- We win.

318
00:24:31,246 --> 00:24:33,382
(Police)

319
00:24:33,382 --> 00:24:35,150
- If we fight.
- We win.

320
00:24:35,150 --> 00:24:37,286
- A beating.
- Is the solution.

321
00:24:37,286 --> 00:24:39,021
- If we fight.
- We win.

322
00:24:39,021 --> 00:24:41,189
- A beating.
- Is the solution.

323
00:24:41,189 --> 00:24:43,358
- If we fight.
- We win.

324
00:24:47,162 --> 00:24:49,164
Control. We're going to need...

325
00:24:50,999 --> 00:24:52,467
a lot more backup.

326
00:24:57,739 --> 00:24:59,408
- Stop right there.
- Would you stop if you were me?

327
00:25:00,742 --> 00:25:02,144
Running won't help you!

328
00:25:04,613 --> 00:25:05,580
Come on.

329
00:25:07,249 --> 00:25:08,350
Seriously.

330
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:27,402
What is this, a farmers' uprising?

331
00:25:27,402 --> 00:25:28,804
Everyone, move! What are you doing here?

332
00:25:28,804 --> 00:25:29,972
Move aside!

333
00:25:34,977 --> 00:25:36,511
This is as far as you go, Mr. Choi.

334
00:25:37,679 --> 00:25:39,247
Mom, it's Dad.

335
00:25:39,881 --> 00:25:40,949
Goodness.

336
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:43,418
Dad, you look like a cop.

337
00:25:44,987 --> 00:25:45,887
So awesome.

338
00:25:50,459 --> 00:25:52,995
Mr. Choi. I've delivered
your true intentions...

339
00:25:52,995 --> 00:25:55,897
to every corner of the village.

340
00:25:57,032 --> 00:26:00,268
Do you think these puppets
can even think properly?

341
00:26:00,902 --> 00:26:02,237
With just a flick of my hand,

342
00:26:02,237 --> 00:26:05,641
I control these people's lives.

343
00:26:05,641 --> 00:26:07,075
(Chief)

344
00:26:10,145 --> 00:26:12,314
It's a good thing I was alone
back then, right?

345
00:26:12,547 --> 00:26:14,983
I should smash you with my fist.

346
00:26:14,983 --> 00:26:16,852
Who are you calling stupid?

347
00:26:16,852 --> 00:26:18,687
You scammer!

348
00:26:18,687 --> 00:26:20,956
You rotten piece of trash!

349
00:26:20,956 --> 00:26:24,126
Did the people of Yeonri-ri
look stupid to you?

350
00:26:24,126 --> 00:26:25,694
Why are you doing this to me?

351
00:26:28,263 --> 00:26:30,132
Oops. I'm sorry.

352
00:26:30,132 --> 00:26:34,569
My foot got stuck right there.

353
00:26:35,237 --> 00:26:37,639
Ten years ago and now,

354
00:26:37,639 --> 00:26:40,809
you've been exploiting the people
of Yeonri-ri for your own good?

355
00:26:40,809 --> 00:26:42,978
Don't go easy on him, Dong Sik.

356
00:26:42,978 --> 00:26:43,946
Of course not.

357
00:26:43,946 --> 00:26:45,047
How dare you!

358
00:26:45,047 --> 00:26:46,148
Call the police!

359
00:26:46,481 --> 00:26:47,849
Call the police!

360
00:26:47,849 --> 00:26:48,850
Sure.

361
00:26:49,451 --> 00:26:50,852
We'll spare your life.

362
00:26:50,852 --> 00:26:53,522
Should we start
by cutting off your right arm?

363
00:26:53,822 --> 00:26:55,991
Everyone, please. Calm down.

364
00:26:56,391 --> 00:26:58,026
Come here. Call a lawyer.

365
00:26:58,026 --> 00:26:59,761
A lawyer.

366
00:26:59,761 --> 00:27:01,396
- Call a lawyer.
- A lawyer?

367
00:27:04,933 --> 00:27:06,034
It won't help.

368
00:27:06,768 --> 00:27:07,769
They not only have evidence,

369
00:27:08,470 --> 00:27:09,671
but also a witness.

370
00:27:10,405 --> 00:27:13,008
You traitor. Do you really think
you'll get away with this?

371
00:27:15,677 --> 00:27:19,014
This is the taste of
Yeonri-ri's ten years of anger.

372
00:27:44,072 --> 00:27:45,173
Ji Gu.

373
00:28:37,125 --> 00:28:38,360
You're here.

374
00:28:39,127 --> 00:28:40,462
Did you bring what I asked for?

375
00:28:50,372 --> 00:28:53,942
They found an excessive amount
of pesticide.

376
00:28:54,910 --> 00:28:57,279
(Written by Seong Tae Hun)

377
00:29:02,084 --> 00:29:02,951
Back then,

378
00:29:04,119 --> 00:29:06,288
I was a researcher who only had
his goal ahead of him in mind.

379
00:29:08,590 --> 00:29:09,625
What in the world is this?

380
00:29:10,525 --> 00:29:13,095
Why is your name on this piece of paper?

381
00:29:13,629 --> 00:29:14,863
What is this? Explain.

382
00:29:16,898 --> 00:29:18,066
Tell me!

383
00:29:25,774 --> 00:29:27,909
(Written by Seong Tae Hun)

384
00:29:28,710 --> 00:29:30,679
This is...

385
00:29:31,313 --> 00:29:34,683
Because of a few words you wrote,

386
00:29:34,683 --> 00:29:38,353
Yeonri-ri's entire harvest was ruined
that year,

387
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:40,255
and people left the village.

388
00:29:41,523 --> 00:29:43,859
I traveled all over the country
trying to resolve it,

389
00:29:43,859 --> 00:29:45,427
and during that time,
my wife got cancer...

390
00:29:51,900 --> 00:29:55,771
Please let it be inspected again.

391
00:29:57,339 --> 00:29:59,441
You shouldn't do this to other people.

392
00:30:00,342 --> 00:30:02,277
Our cabbages are clean.

393
00:30:02,277 --> 00:30:03,679
Please give us another chance.

394
00:30:03,679 --> 00:30:04,579
(Mat Story deceived
the farmers of Yeonri-ri)

395
00:30:06,448 --> 00:30:09,618
I never imagined Mr. Choi
would swap out...

396
00:30:09,618 --> 00:30:10,752
the cabbage samples.

397
00:30:14,323 --> 00:30:16,758
And I never dreamed the words I wrote,
trusting my beliefs...

398
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:20,262
would become a blade...

399
00:30:20,262 --> 00:30:21,296
that'd strangle you and Yeonri-ri.

400
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:26,101
I'm sorry.

401
00:30:41,450 --> 00:30:42,951
(Analysis Report)

402
00:30:43,885 --> 00:30:45,487
(Written by Seong Tae Hun)

403
00:30:48,290 --> 00:30:50,859
But this could still be used as evidence.

404
00:30:51,493 --> 00:30:53,829
What evidence? I trust you.

405
00:30:56,999 --> 00:30:58,934
What kind of fool would go through
all that trouble to save a land,

406
00:30:58,934 --> 00:31:01,303
only to destroy it again
with his own hands?

407
00:31:04,206 --> 00:31:05,407
Let's burn away everything...

408
00:31:06,008 --> 00:31:07,609
from ten years ago with this.

409
00:31:09,378 --> 00:31:11,246
I know how hard you worked...

410
00:31:12,881 --> 00:31:14,716
to save Yeonri-ri's cabbages.

411
00:31:17,219 --> 00:31:18,253
That's enough for me.

412
00:31:21,757 --> 00:31:22,658
I must go...

413
00:31:23,659 --> 00:31:25,360
and finish this once and for all.

414
00:31:27,863 --> 00:31:28,797
I'll make sure...

415
00:31:29,765 --> 00:31:32,200
this land is returned to Yeonri-ri.

416
00:31:34,803 --> 00:31:35,704
But...

417
00:31:37,439 --> 00:31:38,674
once I go back to Seoul this time,

418
00:31:40,342 --> 00:31:41,810
I don't think I'll be able to come back.

419
00:31:51,386 --> 00:31:52,354
Thank you...

420
00:31:53,155 --> 00:31:54,256
for everything.

421
00:32:00,329 --> 00:32:01,263
Me too.

422
00:32:03,465 --> 00:32:04,466
Thank you.

423
00:32:11,340 --> 00:32:12,908
It's all done now.

424
00:32:12,908 --> 00:32:15,077
Your debt's been paid,
so go back to farming.

425
00:32:16,511 --> 00:32:17,279
What?

426
00:32:17,980 --> 00:32:20,782
As a farmer, you cultivate the land.

427
00:32:20,782 --> 00:32:23,118
As a father, you cultivate your family.

428
00:32:24,086 --> 00:32:26,021
There are a lot of people waiting for you
at home right now.

429
00:32:32,427 --> 00:32:33,228
Here he comes.

430
00:32:35,530 --> 00:32:37,366
- You scared me.
- Dad.

431
00:32:37,699 --> 00:32:38,567
Honey.

432
00:32:40,035 --> 00:32:40,902
What?

433
00:32:42,537 --> 00:32:43,872
What is all this?

434
00:32:44,206 --> 00:32:45,974
Good job, honey.

435
00:32:47,242 --> 00:32:49,077
You caught the bad guy, right, Dad?

436
00:32:49,311 --> 00:32:51,413
- Well...
- So that was all an act?

437
00:32:52,481 --> 00:32:53,515
I got goosebumps.

438
00:32:53,982 --> 00:32:55,150
I had faith in you, Dad.

439
00:32:55,584 --> 00:32:58,120
Thank you for trusting me
and waiting, son.

440
00:32:58,587 --> 00:33:00,989
Ji Gu has something for you.

441
00:33:00,989 --> 00:33:03,091
- What?
- Here, Dad.

442
00:33:04,626 --> 00:33:06,461
What's this?

443
00:33:06,828 --> 00:33:09,798
Thank you for being our dad.

444
00:33:09,798 --> 00:33:12,034
You are the hero of our family.

445
00:33:12,267 --> 00:33:13,502
Goodness.

446
00:33:13,969 --> 00:33:15,704
You're not just a hero in the village.

447
00:33:16,071 --> 00:33:19,207
You're a hero in this family too.

448
00:33:22,244 --> 00:33:23,545
I was able to get through it all...

449
00:33:24,913 --> 00:33:26,048
thanks to all of you.

450
00:33:28,684 --> 00:33:29,618
I love you.

451
00:33:31,920 --> 00:33:33,055
I love you.

452
00:33:34,623 --> 00:33:36,325
Where's our youngest?

453
00:33:36,325 --> 00:33:37,559
Ji Gu.

454
00:33:37,559 --> 00:33:42,130
I love you, Ji Gu.

455
00:33:47,436 --> 00:33:49,771
(Mat Story)

456
00:34:07,623 --> 00:34:08,590
I, Seong Tae Hun,

457
00:34:09,091 --> 00:34:11,793
fought my way here
by taking on one guy at a time.

458
00:34:14,162 --> 00:34:15,664
Now, I'm going to reap...

459
00:34:16,765 --> 00:34:17,733
what...

460
00:34:18,667 --> 00:34:19,768
I've sown.

461
00:34:28,277 --> 00:34:31,680
As you know, the third factory project...

462
00:34:31,680 --> 00:34:34,816
is something we have been preparing
for a long time...

463
00:34:35,717 --> 00:34:37,085
(2026 Annual Board Meeting
and General Shareholders' Meeting)

464
00:34:42,557 --> 00:34:43,492
What?

465
00:34:44,426 --> 00:34:45,460
What's he doing?

466
00:34:48,630 --> 00:34:50,599
What is he doing
in the middle of a meeting?

467
00:35:03,211 --> 00:35:05,547
Mr. Seong. What do you think you're doing?

468
00:35:06,014 --> 00:35:06,848
Mr. Bae.

469
00:35:08,150 --> 00:35:09,384
This is my answer.

470
00:35:10,118 --> 00:35:11,186
What?

471
00:35:11,186 --> 00:35:12,521
This cabbage here...

472
00:35:13,355 --> 00:35:15,324
I grew it myself.

473
00:35:15,891 --> 00:35:16,925
On the very land...

474
00:35:17,492 --> 00:35:20,295
in Yeonri-ri that Mr. Choi claimed
was unsuitable for farming.

475
00:35:22,030 --> 00:35:22,965
Take a look.

476
00:35:23,265 --> 00:35:25,901
It didn't die. It's grown this well.

477
00:35:30,505 --> 00:35:31,907
While this may be
Mr. Choi's personal crime,

478
00:35:32,874 --> 00:35:34,376
the company also bears responsibility.

479
00:35:35,544 --> 00:35:36,511
Please return...

480
00:35:37,779 --> 00:35:39,615
the land to the farmers of Yeonri-ri.

481
00:35:40,482 --> 00:35:41,617
I beg you.

482
00:35:52,894 --> 00:35:54,863
(Mat Story)

483
00:35:59,301 --> 00:36:01,637
The third factory project has been halted.

484
00:36:01,937 --> 00:36:03,939
It also put me
in quite a difficult position.

485
00:36:04,673 --> 00:36:06,942
- I'm sorry.
- Did it sound like I was scolding you?

486
00:36:09,611 --> 00:36:11,513
I was actually praising your contribution.

487
00:36:12,047 --> 00:36:13,115
Pardon?

488
00:36:13,115 --> 00:36:14,650
I've told you many times already.

489
00:36:15,417 --> 00:36:18,420
I act in the company's best interest.

490
00:36:19,488 --> 00:36:22,291
Mr. Choi was a parasite
eating away at the company's profits.

491
00:36:23,258 --> 00:36:24,926
I'm glad it finally came to light.

492
00:36:26,228 --> 00:36:28,463
That stubborn integrity
and persistence of yours...

493
00:36:28,463 --> 00:36:29,698
finally paid off.

494
00:36:29,698 --> 00:36:32,334
By the way, where are we headed, Mr. Bae?

495
00:36:41,276 --> 00:36:43,045
What do you think? Do you like it?

496
00:36:45,347 --> 00:36:48,016
Now you should put that stubbornness
and persistence to even greater use.

497
00:36:48,350 --> 00:36:49,318
Isn't that right,

498
00:36:49,851 --> 00:36:50,986
Director Seong Tae Hun?

499
00:36:58,927 --> 00:37:01,730
(Director Seong Tae Hun)

500
00:37:16,945 --> 00:37:19,881
(One year later)

501
00:37:19,881 --> 00:37:24,019
Mat Story's kimchi has recorded
a 38% net profit this year.

502
00:37:24,019 --> 00:37:26,388
It's ranked first in premium kimchi sales.

503
00:37:26,388 --> 00:37:27,756
What's your secret?

504
00:37:28,657 --> 00:37:31,593
The taste of kimchi depends
on the cabbage.

505
00:37:31,827 --> 00:37:33,829
We started from the seeds...

506
00:37:33,829 --> 00:37:35,764
and grew the seedlings ourselves...

507
00:37:35,764 --> 00:37:39,101
in order to focus on developing
our own single cabbage variety...

508
00:37:39,101 --> 00:37:40,335
unique to Mat Story.

509
00:37:40,335 --> 00:37:43,171
So, would you say the cabbage variety...

510
00:37:43,171 --> 00:37:45,574
is the most important factor?

511
00:37:54,583 --> 00:37:57,352
(Yeonri-ri)

512
00:38:01,823 --> 00:38:03,692
- You're here.
- Yes, I'm here.

513
00:38:04,092 --> 00:38:06,161
Right. I'm going to send a picture
to Ji Cheon.

514
00:38:06,161 --> 00:38:07,396
Shall we take a selfie together?

515
00:38:07,396 --> 00:38:08,630
- That sounds great.
- Is that okay?

516
00:38:08,630 --> 00:38:10,499
One, two, three.

517
00:38:14,436 --> 00:38:15,604
Ji Cheon.

518
00:38:15,604 --> 00:38:18,307
The people of Yeonri-ri are doing well.

519
00:38:19,174 --> 00:38:21,443
They're as cheerful and lively as ever.

520
00:38:21,443 --> 00:38:22,577
(Ji Cheon)

521
00:38:22,577 --> 00:38:23,512
Just like always, right?

522
00:38:23,512 --> 00:38:24,279
He's on.

523
00:38:24,279 --> 00:38:28,250
Mat Story's kimchi has recorded
a 38% net profit this year.

524
00:38:28,684 --> 00:38:30,719
It's ranked first in premium kimchi sales.

525
00:38:30,719 --> 00:38:32,154
Overseas exports have also
more than doubled.

526
00:38:32,154 --> 00:38:35,123
Mr. Seong really made it.
He's even on TV now.

527
00:38:35,924 --> 00:38:37,392
He looks handsome.

528
00:38:37,392 --> 00:38:39,928
- He looks great on screen.
- The camera loves him.

529
00:38:39,928 --> 00:38:41,096
Be quiet!

530
00:38:41,096 --> 00:38:42,631
- I can't hear.
- Grew the seedlings ourselves...

531
00:38:42,631 --> 00:38:44,800
in order to focus on developing
our own single cabbage variety...

532
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:47,235
Look at the headlines at the bottom.

533
00:38:47,669 --> 00:38:50,539
Korean cabbage riding
the wave of globalization.

534
00:38:50,539 --> 00:38:52,474
Featured at a royal banquet.

535
00:38:52,474 --> 00:38:54,376
It was featured at a banquet.

536
00:38:55,043 --> 00:38:57,613
With the cabbage
that Manager Seong developed.

537
00:38:57,613 --> 00:38:59,281
He's a director now.

538
00:38:59,615 --> 00:39:00,882
He's a director, not a manager.

539
00:39:01,149 --> 00:39:03,151
I helped grow that cabbage too.

540
00:39:03,151 --> 00:39:04,519
Sure.

541
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:05,954
Our cabbages...

542
00:39:05,954 --> 00:39:08,323
are grown in Simwoo-myeon, Yeonri-ri.

543
00:39:08,323 --> 00:39:09,658
There it is!

544
00:39:09,658 --> 00:39:10,993
He mentioned Yeonri-ri on TV.

545
00:39:11,760 --> 00:39:14,596
I couldn't have done it alone.

546
00:39:16,198 --> 00:39:19,368
I did this together...

547
00:39:19,368 --> 00:39:21,436
with the people of Yeonri-ri.

548
00:39:22,537 --> 00:39:24,706
That's right!

549
00:39:24,706 --> 00:39:26,541
Director Seong is so eloquent.

550
00:39:27,676 --> 00:39:29,411
Has Mr. Seong contacted you
separately, Chief?

551
00:39:29,845 --> 00:39:31,713
No.

552
00:39:31,713 --> 00:39:33,749
Once a person leaves,
they should just keep moving forward.

553
00:39:35,317 --> 00:39:36,852
Why would he look back on Yeonri-ri?

554
00:39:38,920 --> 00:39:42,791
It looks like he's the one
who's looking back.

555
00:39:42,791 --> 00:39:43,825
Don't cry.

556
00:39:46,261 --> 00:39:47,729
Except the village chief.

557
00:40:06,648 --> 00:40:07,482
Hold on.

558
00:40:15,557 --> 00:40:16,458
Good job.

559
00:40:17,059 --> 00:40:18,160
Finish slicing it.

560
00:40:18,527 --> 00:40:19,528
Okay, chef.

561
00:40:26,935 --> 00:40:29,805
Everything seems great in Yeonri-ri.

562
00:40:32,407 --> 00:40:33,408
As for our family...

563
00:40:40,682 --> 00:40:43,752
Do you want me to buy seeds again?

564
00:40:45,954 --> 00:40:46,888
Forget it.

565
00:40:47,956 --> 00:40:50,058
By the time I get back
from two academies, it's late.

566
00:40:50,892 --> 00:40:52,427
I can't take care of it anyway.

567
00:40:54,696 --> 00:40:55,530
Mom.

568
00:40:56,264 --> 00:40:58,634
This place feels like...

569
00:40:59,167 --> 00:41:01,703
even the sunlight and wind are fake
for the peas to grow.

570
00:41:21,923 --> 00:41:22,724
You're home.

571
00:41:23,425 --> 00:41:24,660
Yes. Are you making something?

572
00:41:25,394 --> 00:41:26,762
I just felt like making it again.

573
00:41:33,969 --> 00:41:34,836
You don't like it?

574
00:41:35,470 --> 00:41:36,438
It's good,

575
00:41:37,205 --> 00:41:38,941
but it tastes a bit different
from last year.

576
00:41:47,616 --> 00:41:48,517
It's cold.

577
00:41:50,218 --> 00:41:52,387
It feels colder here
than it did in the fields of Yeonri-ri.

578
00:41:59,828 --> 00:42:02,097
Dad keeps saying it's cold.

579
00:42:11,506 --> 00:42:14,343
He must feel cold in the heart.

580
00:42:18,714 --> 00:42:20,082
The English camp announcement is out.

581
00:42:20,816 --> 00:42:22,551
- You're all applying, right?
- Of course.

582
00:42:22,551 --> 00:42:24,620
And as for Mom...

583
00:42:24,620 --> 00:42:27,155
Including a barbecue party and a musical?

584
00:42:27,155 --> 00:42:28,490
That's a good price.

585
00:42:28,490 --> 00:42:30,125
- It's great.
- It only costs $10,000.

586
00:42:30,359 --> 00:42:33,128
The cost is about $10,000,
including everything?

587
00:42:34,029 --> 00:42:35,998
Mi Ryeo. What's on your mind?

588
00:42:37,299 --> 00:42:38,133
Sorry?

589
00:42:39,267 --> 00:42:40,769
What did you say?

590
00:42:41,436 --> 00:42:44,072
Are you going to sign them up
for the English camp?

591
00:42:53,282 --> 00:42:54,149
Mom.

592
00:42:54,716 --> 00:42:55,751
If I'm not a doctor,

593
00:42:57,152 --> 00:42:58,654
am I not your son anymore?

594
00:42:59,388 --> 00:43:01,323
You came to Seoul without asking too.

595
00:43:02,658 --> 00:43:04,226
Did you ask us for our opinions, Dad?

596
00:43:05,027 --> 00:43:07,296
You said "let's go" so we came here,
the middle of nowhere.

597
00:43:07,729 --> 00:43:08,964
Just because I'm her mom,

598
00:43:09,564 --> 00:43:11,600
does that mean I have
the blueprint of her life?

599
00:43:13,869 --> 00:43:16,138
I tried everything too.

600
00:43:16,905 --> 00:43:18,106
"Listen to me."

601
00:43:18,106 --> 00:43:19,374
"Do it my way."

602
00:43:20,375 --> 00:43:21,576
But in the end,

603
00:43:22,477 --> 00:43:24,613
Bo Mi felt suffocated,

604
00:43:26,214 --> 00:43:29,551
and I was rotting away inside too.

605
00:43:29,551 --> 00:43:31,119
Honey, what's wrong?

606
00:43:36,725 --> 00:43:39,328
Would the kids want this?

607
00:43:43,765 --> 00:43:46,168
Isn't it a waste
for both our kids' lives and mine,

608
00:43:46,735 --> 00:43:48,203
to just dance...

609
00:43:48,971 --> 00:43:50,539
to someone else's tune?

610
00:43:52,441 --> 00:43:53,642
I'll get going now.

611
00:43:53,642 --> 00:43:55,143
- Just like that?
- Just like that?

612
00:43:55,944 --> 00:43:57,713
- What's wrong?
- You're really leaving?

613
00:43:59,481 --> 00:44:01,049
- Why has she changed so much?
- Mi Ryeo.

614
00:44:01,049 --> 00:44:03,185
- She's changed.
- Is something wrong?

615
00:44:03,185 --> 00:44:05,487
- You're really leaving?
- Something must've happened.

616
00:44:06,922 --> 00:44:09,224
(Director Seong Tae Hun)

617
00:44:10,359 --> 00:44:11,593
These are the new candidate
production sites.

618
00:44:11,593 --> 00:44:13,261
This time we focused on Jeollanam-do.

619
00:44:32,414 --> 00:44:33,415
I did it.

620
00:44:33,949 --> 00:44:35,984
I pooped all this by myself.

621
00:44:35,984 --> 00:44:37,085
Fart.

622
00:44:47,796 --> 00:44:50,165
I'm sorry, Chief. Please help me.

623
00:44:50,165 --> 00:44:50,999
Chief.

624
00:44:57,339 --> 00:45:00,108
Mr. Jeong. Have you ever been drenched
with water out in the fields?

625
00:45:00,876 --> 00:45:01,710
Pardon?

626
00:45:02,878 --> 00:45:03,779
Never mind.

627
00:45:06,848 --> 00:45:07,683
Mr. Seong.

628
00:45:08,617 --> 00:45:10,786
About the business trip
to Japan next month...

629
00:45:10,986 --> 00:45:12,220
Right.

630
00:45:12,220 --> 00:45:15,223
It'll be tight to go through
all the investor meetings.

631
00:45:16,792 --> 00:45:19,328
I'd like to go with you and learn.

632
00:45:19,328 --> 00:45:22,331
You're the role model
for us regular employees.

633
00:45:27,302 --> 00:45:28,270
All I did...

634
00:45:30,138 --> 00:45:33,175
was study cabbage for over 20 years.

635
00:45:33,175 --> 00:45:34,543
Come on.

636
00:45:34,543 --> 00:45:36,445
You resolved the Yeonri-ri situation...

637
00:45:37,446 --> 00:45:38,680
and earned recognition.

638
00:45:39,181 --> 00:45:40,449
I'm so jealous.

639
00:45:42,250 --> 00:45:45,520
Doesn't it feel suffocating
here sometimes?

640
00:46:09,578 --> 00:46:10,445
Seong Tae Hun.

641
00:46:24,192 --> 00:46:25,093
Seong Tae Hun.

642
00:46:25,794 --> 00:46:26,995
What are you doing over there?

643
00:46:28,130 --> 00:46:29,164
Don't you miss me?

644
00:46:33,735 --> 00:46:34,536
Ta da.

645
00:46:37,572 --> 00:46:38,907
That's how it is in Yeonri-ri.

646
00:46:39,675 --> 00:46:41,743
They live with their lives laid bare
like this,

647
00:46:41,743 --> 00:46:44,046
so how could I possibly turn
my back on them?

648
00:46:44,680 --> 00:46:46,915
Why are you going this far?

649
00:46:47,449 --> 00:46:50,052
I'm doing this as a resident of Yeonri-ri,

650
00:46:50,052 --> 00:46:51,653
not as a Mat Story employee.

651
00:46:53,956 --> 00:46:55,090
It's coming back to life.

652
00:46:55,090 --> 00:46:56,825
It's good now.

653
00:46:57,993 --> 00:46:59,461
Seong Tae Hun and I did it.

654
00:47:00,095 --> 00:47:01,363
Seong Tae Hun and I did it.

655
00:47:03,432 --> 00:47:05,567
I trust you, Seong Tae Hun.

656
00:47:06,201 --> 00:47:07,970
The soil in Yeonri-ri is heavy.

657
00:47:08,470 --> 00:47:09,771
Your feet sink deep into it.

658
00:47:10,305 --> 00:47:12,441
- Cross.
- Even if you shake it off, it clings.

659
00:47:13,275 --> 00:47:14,843
I, Im Ju Hyeong, chose him.

660
00:47:14,843 --> 00:47:16,345
This man is a resident of Yeonri-ri
from now on.

661
00:47:16,345 --> 00:47:18,180
So joyous

662
00:47:18,180 --> 00:47:20,315
The rising star of Yeonri-ri.

663
00:47:23,151 --> 00:47:23,986
Seong Tae Hun.

664
00:47:24,653 --> 00:47:25,988
Let's have a drink with some side dishes.

665
00:47:44,239 --> 00:47:45,007
Well...

666
00:47:48,977 --> 00:47:49,978
I'm thinking...

667
00:47:51,647 --> 00:47:52,447
of going back...

668
00:47:53,482 --> 00:47:54,383
to Yeonri-ri.

669
00:47:55,317 --> 00:47:56,385
- Dad?
- Will you grow cabbages again?

670
00:47:56,385 --> 00:47:57,286
Honey.

671
00:47:57,286 --> 00:47:59,655
I haven't fully decided yet.

672
00:48:00,389 --> 00:48:01,290
But...

673
00:48:02,824 --> 00:48:04,226
I want to farm.

674
00:48:06,194 --> 00:48:08,130
The first time we went to Yeonri-ri,

675
00:48:08,130 --> 00:48:10,599
you came because of my job.

676
00:48:13,201 --> 00:48:14,136
This time,

677
00:48:14,670 --> 00:48:16,571
I won't force that choice on you.

678
00:48:18,707 --> 00:48:20,842
You can come with me to Yeonri-ri,

679
00:48:21,276 --> 00:48:22,244
or you can stay here.

680
00:48:22,978 --> 00:48:26,048
Whatever you choose, I'll respect it.

681
00:48:27,416 --> 00:48:28,383
Honey.

682
00:48:29,651 --> 00:48:31,386
I thought we were finally
going to live together.

683
00:48:31,386 --> 00:48:32,688
And now you want to be apart again?

684
00:48:32,921 --> 00:48:35,490
Aren't you deciding this too quickly?

685
00:48:38,894 --> 00:48:39,728
No.

686
00:48:41,229 --> 00:48:42,197
I'm going back...

687
00:48:43,131 --> 00:48:44,800
to the time when I was most myself.

688
00:48:46,101 --> 00:48:47,636
When I was truly Seong Tae Hun.

689
00:48:51,173 --> 00:48:52,107
Would...

690
00:48:54,710 --> 00:48:55,677
that be okay?

691
00:49:13,662 --> 00:49:16,098
(Resignation letter)

692
00:49:16,098 --> 00:49:17,432
You told me...

693
00:49:18,367 --> 00:49:21,103
this fountain pen would help me
make the right choices.

694
00:49:22,537 --> 00:49:25,374
With this pen, I made
the best choices I could,

695
00:49:26,141 --> 00:49:28,477
and I've made my final decision as well.

696
00:49:31,313 --> 00:49:32,180
I will...

697
00:49:33,148 --> 00:49:34,449
return it now.

698
00:49:36,018 --> 00:49:38,654
Thank you for everything.

699
00:50:13,121 --> 00:50:14,122
Chief.

700
00:50:16,858 --> 00:50:18,126
I must be hearing things again.

701
00:50:24,433 --> 00:50:25,467
Chief.

702
00:50:34,009 --> 00:50:36,378
How have you been, Chief?

703
00:50:44,219 --> 00:50:45,587
- Chief.
- Chief.

704
00:50:46,021 --> 00:50:48,056
Hi, Chief!

705
00:50:48,056 --> 00:50:49,491
We missed you.

706
00:50:49,491 --> 00:50:51,259
It's been a while, Chief.

707
00:50:51,259 --> 00:50:52,628
- Hello.
- Chief.

708
00:50:55,931 --> 00:50:57,265
This time, it's real.

709
00:50:58,934 --> 00:51:00,535
I'm going to live by working the soil.

710
00:51:01,470 --> 00:51:02,738
Sell this land to me.

711
00:51:19,621 --> 00:51:20,756
Ji Cheon.

712
00:51:20,756 --> 00:51:21,857
Bo Mi.

713
00:51:25,127 --> 00:51:25,994
Bo Mi.

714
00:51:26,428 --> 00:51:28,630
What are you doing here
without any notice?

715
00:51:28,630 --> 00:51:29,464
I wanted to surprise you.

716
00:51:34,202 --> 00:51:36,138
The marigold you gave me...

717
00:51:36,438 --> 00:51:37,572
I took good care of it.

718
00:51:39,741 --> 00:51:41,576
This is the first flower from the pot.

719
00:51:41,977 --> 00:51:42,878
Are you serious?

720
00:51:46,949 --> 00:51:48,050
It's so beautiful.

721
00:51:51,787 --> 00:51:52,654
Bo Mi.

722
00:51:54,423 --> 00:51:56,491
I studied hard in Seoul.

723
00:51:58,226 --> 00:52:01,630
But it felt like I was missing something.

724
00:52:04,066 --> 00:52:05,901
I want to laugh...

725
00:52:05,901 --> 00:52:07,235
and be happy with you.

726
00:52:08,503 --> 00:52:10,439
Taking my time and not rushing things,

727
00:52:12,240 --> 00:52:13,475
while growing on my own.

728
00:52:16,244 --> 00:52:17,746
I missed you so much.

729
00:52:21,883 --> 00:52:23,185
I missed you too.

730
00:52:27,189 --> 00:52:28,924
(Coal Museum)

731
00:52:28,924 --> 00:52:30,158
I'll check your tickets.

732
00:52:30,158 --> 00:52:31,693
Please head inside.

733
00:52:31,693 --> 00:52:32,794
Thank you.

734
00:52:32,794 --> 00:52:33,795
Hello.

735
00:52:35,497 --> 00:52:36,999
How fun.

736
00:52:36,999 --> 00:52:38,934
I've missed you, Yeonri-ri.

737
00:52:44,072 --> 00:52:45,140
Seong Ji Gu.

738
00:52:46,742 --> 00:52:48,110
You're finally behaving like a young kid.

739
00:53:02,224 --> 00:53:03,258
How have you been,

740
00:53:04,126 --> 00:53:05,327
Seong Ji Sang?

741
00:53:07,029 --> 00:53:08,764
Hey, Han Wu Ju.

742
00:53:10,265 --> 00:53:12,067
I've been well.

743
00:53:14,236 --> 00:53:15,771
Have you been well?

744
00:53:18,373 --> 00:53:19,207
No.

745
00:53:19,841 --> 00:53:20,809
I...

746
00:53:24,112 --> 00:53:26,248
kind of missed you.

747
00:53:31,420 --> 00:53:32,154
Me?

748
00:53:35,590 --> 00:53:37,025
It's your first time here, right?

749
00:53:37,726 --> 00:53:39,428
I'll show you something great.

750
00:53:45,400 --> 00:53:46,401
How far does it go up?

751
00:53:46,401 --> 00:53:47,903
Look at the view.

752
00:53:50,906 --> 00:53:53,208
(Yeonri-ri Village Hall)

753
00:53:53,208 --> 00:53:55,711
Ladies, did you upload
the cabbage pictures?

754
00:53:55,711 --> 00:53:57,479
- Yes.
- Now, down here...

755
00:53:57,479 --> 00:53:59,348
This is the most important part.

756
00:53:59,348 --> 00:54:00,382
Look here.

757
00:54:00,382 --> 00:54:03,785
You see this hashtag symbol?
This is very important.

758
00:54:03,785 --> 00:54:05,354
Hashtag.

759
00:54:05,354 --> 00:54:07,255
Hashtag.

760
00:54:07,255 --> 00:54:09,257
Hashtag.

761
00:54:09,257 --> 00:54:11,326
Hashtag, sharp!

762
00:54:11,560 --> 00:54:14,262
Hashtag, sharp!

763
00:54:15,230 --> 00:54:17,799
If you look here,
there's the hashtag symbol.

764
00:54:17,799 --> 00:54:21,103
Hashtag Yeonri-ri cabbage.

765
00:54:21,103 --> 00:54:24,139
Yeonri-ri cabbage.

766
00:54:24,139 --> 00:54:26,942
Hashtag super delicious.

767
00:54:26,942 --> 00:54:30,712
Super delicious.

768
00:54:30,712 --> 00:54:31,713
Delicious.

769
00:54:31,713 --> 00:54:32,648
Post it.

770
00:54:32,648 --> 00:54:33,715
Post it.

771
00:54:33,715 --> 00:54:35,317
That's too casual.

772
00:54:35,317 --> 00:54:36,585
Please post it.

773
00:54:38,053 --> 00:54:39,621
You got it?

774
00:54:41,056 --> 00:54:42,858
Post it.

775
00:54:46,261 --> 00:54:47,362
Hello?

776
00:54:48,664 --> 00:54:49,698
Yes.

777
00:54:49,698 --> 00:54:50,732
This is she.

778
00:54:53,035 --> 00:54:53,869
Yes.

779
00:54:54,770 --> 00:54:55,904
Are you serious?

780
00:54:57,606 --> 00:54:58,473
Okay.

781
00:54:58,774 --> 00:54:59,808
Thank you!

782
00:55:00,609 --> 00:55:02,177
My goodness.

783
00:55:02,744 --> 00:55:05,714
Those scammers were arrested!

784
00:55:10,485 --> 00:55:13,088
- That's great news.
- What a relief.

785
00:55:16,525 --> 00:55:18,560
Thank you so much.

786
00:55:24,199 --> 00:55:26,234
- Thank you.
- Enjoy your meal.

787
00:55:36,511 --> 00:55:38,080
- Here you go.
- Ji Cheon.

788
00:55:43,018 --> 00:55:44,486
Did you make this?

789
00:55:45,921 --> 00:55:46,888
Try it.

790
00:56:00,002 --> 00:56:02,337
You shouldn't be working part-time here.

791
00:56:02,337 --> 00:56:03,605
You should open your own place instead.

792
00:56:05,207 --> 00:56:07,576
I've actually been keeping an eye out
for a spot.

793
00:56:07,776 --> 00:56:09,244
This is a food startup theme park.

794
00:56:09,878 --> 00:56:11,380
So I thought it'd be
a good place to start.

795
00:56:11,380 --> 00:56:12,581
Totally!

796
00:56:12,948 --> 00:56:15,984
Have you thought of a name for the store?

797
00:56:17,352 --> 00:56:18,387
Spring.

798
00:56:19,187 --> 00:56:20,155
Spring?

799
00:56:21,123 --> 00:56:22,357
Yes. Spring.

800
00:56:23,325 --> 00:56:24,226
Spring?

801
00:56:28,230 --> 00:56:30,265
(Yeonri-ri)

802
00:56:33,468 --> 00:56:37,906
(Seong Tae Hun's field)

803
00:56:39,908 --> 00:56:41,743
(May you only walk the right path)

804
00:56:41,743 --> 00:56:43,378
(Agriculture is the foundation
of the nation)

805
00:56:44,546 --> 00:56:46,381
(May you only walk the right path)

806
00:57:01,530 --> 00:57:04,099
Attention, everyone.

807
00:57:05,033 --> 00:57:06,301
Today...

808
00:57:06,301 --> 00:57:08,704
marks the day...

809
00:57:09,137 --> 00:57:12,207
when Yeonri-ri's smartest
yet most stubborn farmer,

810
00:57:12,207 --> 00:57:15,410
Seong Tae Hun, returns to the soil.

811
00:57:15,410 --> 00:57:16,345
Applause!

812
00:57:18,580 --> 00:57:20,382
You're the best, Dad!

813
00:57:22,451 --> 00:57:23,485
There was no need for a ceremony.

814
00:57:23,485 --> 00:57:25,954
I was just going to start quietly.

815
00:57:25,954 --> 00:57:27,022
Why keep it quiet?

816
00:57:27,389 --> 00:57:29,057
It's your fresh start.

817
00:57:29,057 --> 00:57:31,226
Of course, we must celebrate.

818
00:57:33,362 --> 00:57:35,631
I'm going to post this, okay?

819
00:57:40,402 --> 00:57:42,204
Then...

820
00:57:42,204 --> 00:57:45,374
take this.

821
00:57:45,907 --> 00:57:47,442
Three bows!

822
00:57:47,442 --> 00:57:49,711
Three bows!

823
00:57:52,314 --> 00:57:53,148
Over here.

824
00:57:54,016 --> 00:57:54,816
Over here too.

825
00:57:56,985 --> 00:57:58,820
Ladies and gentlemen of Yeonri-ri.

826
00:57:59,688 --> 00:58:01,089
This year,

827
00:58:01,089 --> 00:58:03,158
I'm planning to grow chili peppers here.

828
00:58:03,992 --> 00:58:06,194
Chili peppers are the second
most famous crop in Yeonri-ri...

829
00:58:06,194 --> 00:58:07,262
after cabbage, right?

830
00:58:11,767 --> 00:58:13,402
I'll take care of the watering.

831
00:58:13,602 --> 00:58:16,104
Don't forget you're doing this
with me, Dad.

832
00:58:16,104 --> 00:58:17,372
Don't forget.

833
00:58:17,372 --> 00:58:19,641
You have to pour the water
near the roots.

834
00:58:19,641 --> 00:58:21,009
I read that in a book.

835
00:58:27,182 --> 00:58:30,052
What? They look cute together.

836
00:58:31,386 --> 00:58:33,155
What? Are you jealous?

837
00:58:34,456 --> 00:58:35,424
No way.

838
00:58:36,058 --> 00:58:38,226
Hye Sun. I set a wedding date...

839
00:58:39,561 --> 00:58:40,495
with Wang Dong Sik.

840
00:58:44,599 --> 00:58:45,634
Are you serious?

841
00:58:46,234 --> 00:58:49,171
Yes, we're engaged now.

842
00:58:49,571 --> 00:58:50,539
What?

843
00:58:51,173 --> 00:58:53,175
- Congratulations.
- We'll live happily.

844
00:58:54,576 --> 00:58:55,811
For real, Dong Sik?

845
00:58:57,479 --> 00:58:58,513
I'm so embarrassed.

846
00:58:59,214 --> 00:59:02,384
He can't run away anymore.

847
00:59:02,951 --> 00:59:04,987
He's got his feet in Yeonri-ri's soil now.

848
00:59:04,987 --> 00:59:06,021
He can't run.

849
00:59:06,021 --> 00:59:08,156
Don't even think about running away.

850
00:59:12,928 --> 00:59:15,063
The rough stones of misunderstanding
have been cleared away,

851
00:59:15,063 --> 00:59:17,432
and the weeds of self-blame
have been pulled out.

852
00:59:21,670 --> 00:59:24,539
Now, a firm happiness
that no one can break...

853
00:59:24,539 --> 00:59:26,975
has taken root in Yeonri-ri.

854
00:59:31,580 --> 00:59:34,049
There's only one lesson in farming.

855
00:59:35,984 --> 00:59:37,552
You reap what you sow,

856
00:59:37,552 --> 00:59:39,288
and what you plant is what grows.

857
00:59:43,025 --> 00:59:44,760
It took a long time to realize...

858
00:59:45,494 --> 00:59:48,897
that the heart, like the land, is honest.

859
00:59:50,499 --> 00:59:52,834
Hatred and love alike...

860
00:59:53,335 --> 00:59:54,903
grow just as you plant them.

861
00:59:56,171 --> 00:59:57,472
All right.

862
00:59:57,973 --> 01:00:00,609
We're truly a family now.

863
01:00:06,615 --> 01:00:10,252
Let's yell out our slogan.

864
01:00:10,953 --> 01:00:11,787
All right.

865
01:00:11,787 --> 01:00:14,389
I say, "If you plant it,"

866
01:00:14,389 --> 01:00:16,858
and you say, "It'll grow."

867
01:00:16,858 --> 01:00:17,960
Okay?

868
01:00:17,960 --> 01:00:19,294
Okay.

869
01:00:19,728 --> 01:00:20,729
Let's do this.

870
01:00:21,096 --> 01:00:22,297
If you plant it!

871
01:00:23,231 --> 01:00:25,300
It'll grow!

872
01:00:25,767 --> 01:00:27,169
If you plant it!

873
01:00:27,803 --> 01:00:30,172
It'll grow!

874
01:00:35,277 --> 01:00:36,378
And one more truth...

875
01:00:36,979 --> 01:00:39,047
you come to understand in the end...

876
01:00:40,682 --> 01:00:44,686
Good days will surely come someday.

877
01:00:50,459 --> 01:00:52,127
For those who plant hope,

878
01:00:53,061 --> 01:00:54,029
it'll definitely...

879
01:00:54,763 --> 01:00:56,398
grow!

880
01:00:59,001 --> 01:01:02,838
(Thank you to all the viewers)

881
01:01:02,838 --> 01:01:06,675
(who have loved and supported
Cabbage Your Life.)

882
01:01:31,166 --> 01:01:34,136
(Cabbage Your Life)

883
01:02:04,366 --> 01:02:06,368
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)

